    <node id="char_maxarius">
      <data key="d1">Maxarius</data>
      <data key="d2">[]</data>
      <data key="d3">character</data>
      <data key="d4">first_high_templar</data>
      <data key="d5">Per the Sanctum relic texts (as recounted in the wiki and video), Maxarius, the first High Templar, was in truth Innocence himself - a charlatan who stole the Descry symbol from fire-terrified newcomers, used their fear, and vilified his brother Sin to ascend.</data>
      <data key="d6">["poe1"]</data>
      <data key="d7">branch</data>
      <data key="d8">["sanctum"]</data>
      <data key="d9">azmeri_ezomyte_ancient</data>
      <data key="d10">{"in_world_year": null, "relative": "ancient, when the Azmeri still lived in the Azmerian mountains", "story_order": null}</data>
      <data key="d11">[]</data>
      <data key="d12">canon</data>
      <data key="d13">high</data>
      <data key="d14">[{"source_id": "src_yt_7QuY96FyhG4", "locator": "[28:00]-[30:30] relics reveal Maxarius = Innocence; quote 'a charlatan, a liar and a power seeker'"}, {"source_id": "src_poewiki_history_of_wraeclast", "locator": "===Templar history (line ~188): \"The very first High Templar, Maxarius, was not Innocence's chosen, as was told, but Innocence himself.\""}, {"source_id": "src_poewiki_innocence", "locator": "Lore: \"He posed himself as Maxarius, the first High Templar, and vilified his own brother as the Original Evil.\""}]</data>
      <data key="d15">["leagues_late"]</data>
      <data key="d16">["azmeri_ezomyte_ancient"]</data>
      <data key="d17">["branch"]</data>
