    <node id="char_tecrod">
      <data key="d1">Tecrod</data>
      <data key="d2">["Tecrod, the Hated Slave", "The Hated Slave"]</data>
      <data key="d3">character</data>
      <data key="d4" />
      <data key="d5">'The Hated Slave': Abyssal Lich Lord who, unlike Amanamu, Kurgal and Ulaman, acts independently of Kulemak (PoE1 wiki: forsaken by Kulemak for unclear reasons). In PoE2 (Legacy of the Precursors) he steals the Flame Seed on his wyrm, seeks Kulemak's favour, hunts for the Edicts and is destroyed by the Arbiter of Divinity.</data>
      <data key="d6">["poe1", "poe2"]</data>
      <data key="d7">endgame_plot</data>
      <data key="d8">["poe2_abyss"]</data>
      <data key="d9">poe2_endgame</data>
      <data key="d10">{"in_world_year": null, "relative": null, "story_order": null}</data>
      <data key="d11">[]</data>
      <data key="d12">canon</data>
      <data key="d13">medium</data>
      <data key="d14">[{"source_id": "src_poewiki_the_lightless", "locator": "Abyssal Liches: Tecrod"}, {"source_id": "src_poe2wiki_tecrod", "locator": "page"}, {"source_id": "src_poe2wiki_tecrod", "locator": "Lore: independent of Kulemak; steals Flame Seed; destroyed by Arbiter of Divinity"}, {"source_id": "src_poe2wiki_tecrod", "locator": "Lore"}, {"source_id": "src_poewiki_the_lightless", "locator": "Lich Lords: Tecrod, the disgraced Abyssal Lich, forsaken by Kulemak; freed from a Precursor sarcophagus, seeks to win back Kulemak favour"}]</data>
      <data key="d15">["leagues_early", "poe2_endgame", "twilight_order_edicts"]</data>
      <data key="d16">["poe2_endgame"]</data>
      <data key="d17">["endgame_plot"]</data>
      <data key="d24">[{"domain": "poe2_endgame", "summary": "White-haloed Abyssal Lich Lord ('the Hated Slave'). The PoE2 wiki says that, unlike Amanamu, Kurgal and Ulaman, he acts independently of Kulemak's other lords and is active in the Epilogue hunting the Edicts; the PoE wiki adds he was forsaken by Kulemak, is freed from a Precursor sarcophagus and seeks to win back Kulemak's favour. He steals the Flame Seed, incapacitates the Exile at the Origin Tower claiming the First Edict's power for 'the Master' (probably Kulemak, inferred), and is destroyed by the Arbiter of Divinity."}, {"domain": "twilight_order_edicts", "summary": "Abyssal Lich Lord ('the Hated Slave') with a white halo; unlike Amanamu, Kurgal and Ulaman he acts independently of Kulemak and hunts the Edicts. Appears as a wyrm rider who steals the Flame Seed after the Arbiter of Ash falls; when the Exile places the Origin Core in the Origin Tower his wyrm incapacitates the Exile and he claims the power for 'the Master', but the Arbiter of Divinity destroys his body."}]</data>
      <data key="d18">released</data>
      <data key="d19">11</data>
      <data key="d20">2</data>
      <data key="d21">1</data>
      <data key="d22">1</data>
      <data key="d23">False</data>
    </node>
