    <node id="char_the_hooded_one">
      <data key="d1">The Hooded One</data>
      <data key="d2">["Sin", "Thief of Virtue"]</data>
      <data key="d3">character</data>
      <data key="d4" />
      <data key="d5">Unnamed Hooded One bound by a runed sword in the Grelwood's Tree of Souls, later revealed as Sin (Thief of Virtue) who created the Beast; guides the Exile through Acts 1-3.</data>
      <data key="d6">["poe2"]</data>
      <data key="d7">main_plot</data>
      <data key="d8">[]</data>
      <data key="d9">poe2_campaign</data>
      <data key="d10">{"in_world_year": null, "relative": "", "story_order": null}</data>
      <data key="d11">["act_poe2_act1", "act_poe2_act2", "act_poe2_act3", "act_poe2_act4"]</data>
      <data key="d12">canon</data>
      <data key="d13">medium</data>
      <data key="d14">[{"source_id": "src_poe2wiki_lore", "locator": "Prelude"}, {"source_id": "src_poe2wiki_legacy_of_the_precursors", "locator": "Check on the Hooded One"}, {"source_id": "src_poe2wiki_secrets_in_the_dark", "locator": "Quest 'Speak to Una'"}, {"source_id": "src_poe2wiki_the_trail_of_corruption_act_2", "locator": "Quest log 'Speak to the Hooded One in the Shrine to the Northwest'"}, {"source_id": "src_poewiki_sin", "locator": "Lore section 'The Beast'"}, {"source_id": "src_poe2wiki_the_trail_of_corruption_act_2", "locator": "Quote 'I am the Thief of Virtue. I am Sin.'"}, {"source_id": "src_poe2wiki_the_search", "locator": "Witness the Hooded One"}, {"source_id": "src_poe2wiki_the_trail_of_corruption_act_2", "locator": "Speak to the Hooded One in the Shrine: 'I am... a god. I am the Thief of Virtue. I am Sin.'"}, {"source_id": "src_poe2wiki_the_search", "locator": "Witness The Hooded One"}, {"source_id": "src_poe2wiki_legacy_of_the_vaal", "locator": "dialogue"}]</data>
      <data key="d15">["deep_history", "poe2_acts_1_3", "poe2_acts_4_plus", "twilight_order_edicts", "vaal"]</data>
      <data key="d16">["poe2_campaign"]</data>
      <data key="d17">["main_plot"]</data>
      <data key="d24">[{"domain": "deep_history", "summary": "Dark hooded god-like figure, likely Sin (PoE2 wiki inference), impaled by Count Geonor who takes the Seed of Corruption from him in PoE2's opening cinematic; in the endgame quest Legacy of the Precursors he sleeps in thrall to the Beast's corruption and is the intended wielder of the Precursor Weapon. A YouTube lore creator says Act 4 hints he was once a Precursor (community theory, unconfirmed)."}, {"domain": "poe2_acts_4_plus", "summary": "The god Sin in disguise (identity confessed in Act 2: 'I am the Thief of Virtue. I am Sin'). In Act 4 he reforges the Weapon, recognises Precursor writing from a faded mortal childhood, cures Tavakai and organises the alliance; in the endgame he sleeps under the Beast's Corruption."}, {"domain": "twilight_order_edicts", "summary": "Mysterious guide of the PoE2 Exile, revealed in Act 2 to be the god Sin, the Thief of Virtue and creator of the Beast. Recognises Precursor writing from a mortal childhood memory, forges the Weapon, and in the Epilogue lies in corruption-induced sleep."}, {"domain": "vaal", "summary": "Guide figure in PoE2 who directs the Exile to the Vaal and the weapon."}]</data>
      <data key="d18">released</data>
      <data key="d19">22</data>
      <data key="d20">2</data>
      <data key="d21">1</data>
      <data key="d22">1</data>
      <data key="d23">False</data>
    </node>
    <node id="char_the_king_in_the_mists">
      <data key="d1">The King in the Mists</data>
      <data key="d2">["King in the Mists", "King of the Nameless"]</data>
      <data key="d3">character</data>
      <data key="d4" />
      <data key="d5">Chief of the Nameless shadow creatures in the Viridian Wildwood and enemy of the Maji. Boss of Affliction (PoE1, 3.23) and, in PoE2 Act 1 (Freythorn), the cult 'king' guarding the final Ritual altar. In Legacy of the Maji, Aoife recalls being drawn to him, believing him one of the Maji of old.</data>
      <data key="d6">["poe1", "poe2"]</data>
      <data key="d7">branch</data>
      <data key="d8">["affliction", "ritual"]</data>
      <data key="d9">poe1_leagues</data>
      <data key="d10">{"in_world_year": null, "relative": null, "story_order": null}</data>
      <data key="d11">[]</data>
      <data key="d12">canon</data>
      <data key="d13">medium</data>
      <data key="d14">[{"source_id": "src_poewiki_history_of_wraeclast", "locator": "The Viridian Wildwood section"}, {"source_id": "src_poewiki_affliction_league", "locator": "unique items 'the King in the Mists'"}, {"source_id": "src_poewiki_path_of_exile_settlers_of_kalguur", "locator": "'The King in the Mists encounter added to Ritual'"}, {"source_id": "src_poewiki_history_of_wraeclast", "locator": "section 'The Viridian Wildwood'"}, {"source_id": "src_poewiki_affliction_league", "locator": "Unique items: drops from the King in the Mists"}, {"source_id": "src_poe2wiki_ominous_altars", "locator": "lead/quest"}, {"source_id": "src_poe2wiki_legacy_of_the_maji", "locator": "Aoife dialogue about the King in the Mists"}, {"source_id": "src_poe2wiki_legacy_of_the_maji", "locator": "Aoife: 'You killed him in your domain... but now he returns from his'; step 17 Defeat the King in the Mists; step 20 Pick up the Head of the King"}, {"source_id": "src_ggg_content_update_0_5_0", "locator": "Killing the King drops The Head of the King, which starts the Rite of the Nameless in Caer Tarth"}]</data>
      <data key="d15">["leagues_late", "leagues_mid", "poe2_endgame"]</data>
      <data key="d16">["poe1_leagues", "poe2_campaign", "poe2_endgame"]</data>
      <data key="d17">["branch"]</data>
      <data key="d24">[{"domain": "leagues_late", "summary": "Major antagonist of Affliction league, a shadowy Nameless force within the Viridian Wildwood against whom the Maji wage a long war; later added to Ritual in 3.25."}, {"domain": "poe2_endgame", "summary": "Boss who killed Aoife and whose effigies tether him to the world; killed once in the campaign (Ogham) yet returns in the endgame Ritual quest, where he is fought at the Crux of Nothingness; his Head starts the Rite of the Nameless. Drawing power from the Bodach is a guide claim."}]</data>
      <data key="d18">released</data>
      <data key="d19">15</data>
      <data key="d20">1</data>
      <data key="d21">1</data>
      <data key="d22">1</data>
      <data key="d23">False</data>
    </node>
