    <node id="concept_corruption">
      <data key="d1">Corruption</data>
      <data key="d2">[]</data>
      <data key="d3">concept</data>
      <data key="d4">lore_force</data>
      <data key="d5">Lore force of mutation and malformation tied to the Beast and its predecessors: the Beast 'possesses corrupting powers' that mutate whatever contacts it; Kitava is called 'God of Corruption' in Karui dialogue; Precursors mastered corruption and Doryani attempts to harness the Precursor Weapon to destroy corruption. Not the Corrupted-item mechanic.</data>
      <data key="d6">["poe1", "poe2"]</data>
      <data key="d7">background</data>
      <data key="d8">[]</data>
      <data key="d9">primordial</data>
      <data key="d10">{"in_world_year": null, "relative": "from the Precursor era onward (Beast, Vaal, Eternal Empire)", "story_order": null}</data>
      <data key="d11">[]</data>
      <data key="d12">canon</data>
      <data key="d13">medium</data>
      <data key="d14">[{"source_id": "src_poewiki_the_beast_lore", "locator": "intro: 'The Beast possesses corrupting powers, devouring the souls of his prey and mutating whoever comes in contact with it.'"}, {"source_id": "src_poewiki_karui_gods", "locator": "section '==Kitava==' &gt; Dialogue, Haku's 'Kaom' option: 'Kitava, God of Corruption, consumed Kaom from heart to skin.'"}, {"source_id": "src_poewiki_history_of_wraeclast", "locator": "section '===Precursor civilization===': 'After mastering corruption, they delved deeper...'; the Precursor Weapon is one 'which Doryani attempts to harness to destroy corruption'"}, {"source_id": "src_poewiki_karui_gods", "locator": "Haku dialogue: 'Kitava, God of Corruption'"}, {"source_id": "src_poewiki_sin", "locator": "PoE2 section: 'the Seed of Corruption'"}, {"source_id": "src_poewiki_history_of_wraeclast", "locator": "Vaal temple section: 'worship of Corruption'"}]</data>
      <data key="d15">["gap_deep_history_vaal_precursor_eternal", "gap_isolated_links"]</data>
      <data key="d16">["primordial"]</data>
      <data key="d17">["background"]</data>
      <data key="d24">[{"domain": "gap_isolated_links", "summary": "The in-world corrupting power named by the Karui and Vaal (Kitava as 'God of Corruption', worship of Corruption at a Vaal temple) and carried as the Seed of Corruption (what remains of the Beast) in PoE2. The item-corruption mechanic is a separate game system."}]</data>
      <data key="d18">released</data>
      <data key="d19">15</data>
      <data key="d20">2</data>
      <data key="d21">2</data>
      <data key="d22">2</data>
      <data key="d23">False</data>
    </node>
    <node id="concept_crisis_fragments">
      <data key="d1">Crisis Fragments</data>
      <data key="d2">[]</data>
      <data key="d3">concept</data>
      <data key="d4" />
      <data key="d5">Fragments needed to open the sealed door of the Burning Monolith (Arbiter of Ash). In 0.1-0.4 three were needed (Ancient, Weathered, Faded), one per Citadel boss. In the 0.5 quest log only the Ancient and Weathered fragments are picked up in the Fortress Enigma Chambers; Citadels continue to drop them for repeat runs. Guides disagree on which Citadel drops which (most: Iron=Ancient, Copper=Faded, Stone=Weathered), and the quest log matches that for Geonor (Ancient) and Doryani (Weathered).</data>
      <data key="d6">["poe2"]</data>
      <data key="d7">endgame_plot</data>
      <data key="d8">[]</data>
      <data key="d9">poe2_endgame</data>
      <data key="d10">{"in_world_year": null, "relative": null, "story_order": null}</data>
      <data key="d11">[]</data>
      <data key="d12">canon</data>
      <data key="d13">medium</data>
      <data key="d14">[{"source_id": "src_poe2wiki_the_pinnacle_of_flame", "locator": "Obtain three Crisis Fragments"}, {"source_id": "src_web_timesaver_poe2_citadels", "locator": "Citadel-to-Arbiter loop; fragment mapping disagrees between guides"}]</data>
      <data key="d15">["poe2_endgame"]</data>
      <data key="d16">["poe2_endgame"]</data>
      <data key="d17">["endgame_plot"]</data>
      <data key="d18">released</data>
      <data key="d19">2</data>
      <data key="d20">3</data>
