    <node id="concept_godhood">
      <data key="d1">Nature of godhood (ascension)</data>
      <data key="d2">[]</data>
      <data key="d3">concept</data>
      <data key="d4">cosmology</data>
      <data key="d5">In PoE lore a mortal of rare quality could ascend to godhood on the adoration of their people, shedding mortality; this became impossible once Sin created the Beast. Becoming a god often costs one's humanity. Gods can also be 'made' by belief of followers (Innocence's ascension was fuelled by hatred of Sin).</data>
      <data key="d6">["poe1", "poe2"]</data>
      <data key="d7">background</data>
      <data key="d8">[]</data>
      <data key="d9">primordial</data>
      <data key="d10">{"in_world_year": null, "relative": "before the creation of the Beast", "story_order": null}</data>
      <data key="d11">[]</data>
      <data key="d12">canon</data>
      <data key="d13">high</data>
      <data key="d14">[{"source_id": "src_poewiki_god", "locator": "section 'Ascension to godhood'"}, {"source_id": "src_ingame_sin_dialogue", "locator": "Sin, 'The Origins of the Gods': \"There was a time before the Beast ... men and women like you could ascend. Through rareness of quality and the adoration of their people...\""}]</data>
      <data key="d15">["gods_cosmology"]</data>
      <data key="d16">["primordial"]</data>
      <data key="d17">["background"]</data>
