    <node id="concept_the_edicts">
      <data key="d1">The Edicts (Precursor murals)</data>
      <data key="d2">[]</data>
      <data key="d3">concept</data>
      <data key="d5">Series of vague Precursor murals described by the PoE2 wiki as depicting the Beast and possibly instructions on how to contain it; numbered First to Fourth in game. Known: Third = instrument is the Weapon (Hooded One recognises it as 'the Weapon I saw in that third mural'); Second = Doryani's guess that the Seed was its instrument; Fourth = investigated in the Epilogue after the Arbiter of Ash (PoE1 wiki editors speculate it caused the Great Fire); First = unexplained threat averted in the Epilogue. The full text of the edicts is not given in any source read. Not to be confused with Count Geonor's hanging edicts in Ogham.</data>
      <data key="d6">["poe2"]</data>
      <data key="d7">main_plot</data>
      <data key="d8">[]</data>
      <data key="d9">precursor</data>
      <data key="d10">{"in_world_year": null, "relative": "Precursor age, far older than the Vaal and Winter of the World", "story_order": null}</data>
      <data key="d11">[]</data>
      <data key="d12">canon</data>
      <data key="d13">medium</data>
      <data key="d14">[{"source_id": "src_poe2wiki_the_beast", "locator": "'It was depicted in their Edicts, vague murals that depicts the Beast and possibly instructions on how to contain it.'"}, {"source_id": "src_poe2wiki_the_search", "locator": "Return to Kingsmarch: Doryani 'The Third Edict? What is the meaning... of these Edicts?'"}, {"source_id": "src_poe2wiki_the_search", "locator": "Return to Kingsmarch: Hooded One 'It is the Weapon I saw in that third mural'; Enter the Excavated Site: Makoru 'These murals... appear to depict the Weapon... and the Beast'"}]</data>
      <data key="d15">["twilight_order_edicts"]</data>
      <data key="d16">["precursor"]</data>
      <data key="d17">["main_plot"]</data>
